      "why": "iterative is the lowest-area family (single shared datapath, no per-stage registers). It is the only family here that can plausibly hit >=1 MSPS with a small N: at W~14, N~12 the datapath is short enough that Fmax should exceed ~100 MHz, giving throughput = Fmax/(N+3) >= 1 MSPS. Accuracy at N=12-16 with W=14-16 comfortably exceeds 2^-10. This is where the min-area corner of the front lives, so it gets the largest share."
    },
    {
      "family": "unrolled_k",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "param": "data_width",
          "low": 12,
          "high": 16
        ,
          "choices": null
        },
        {
          "param": "n_iter",
          "low": 10,
          "high": 16
        ,
          "choices": null
        },
        {
          "param": "angle_guard",
          "low": 0,
          "high": 2
        ,
          "choices": null
